---
scope: src/service/install/initContent
status: aligned
description: "Single reader of the canonical doc set for the install subtree, returning content verbatim and owning the registry of named docs and methodology subsets."
intent: >
  initContent is the install subtree's sole reader of canonical content
  and the sole owner of canonical-name lookup. Every install helper that
  needs doctrine asks here by name; nobody else opens canonical files
  themselves. Bytes flow through unmodified — composition, parsing, and
  any transformation belong to the consumer that has the reasoning to
  justify each rewrite. Membership in named subsets like the methodology
  is decided here too, so adding a canonical doc or rescoping a subset
  is a single-file edit and every consumer picks it up on the next init.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - Every install-subtree consumer that needs canonical content asks initContent for it by name. No other helper under the install subtree opens canonical files directly.
    - Returned content is byte-identical to the canonical source. Trimming, reformatting, frontmatter stripping, link rewriting, and section extraction are consumer responsibilities.
    - Named subsets of the canonical content (the methodology subset and any future siblings) are enumerated through this helper. Consumers iterate whatever list comes back rather than maintaining their own membership lists.
    - Missing or unreadable canonical content is a hard, named failure. The helper never substitutes a default, a stub, or empty content to keep the init flowing.
  undesired:
    - A second install-subtree reader of the canonical doc set, regardless of motivation. Multiple readers fork the source-of-truth surface and let "what one helper sees" diverge from "what another helper sees".
    - A consumer maintaining its own list of which docs belong to a named subset. Local membership lists are a second source of truth for the same decision and silently miss the next subset addition.
    - Doc content baked into this helper's source as literals "for performance" or "in case the canonical location moves". The duplicate is the regression the chokepoint exists to prevent.
    - Transformation applied here on behalf of consumers — heading rewrites, frontmatter stripping, link normalization, section extraction. Each transform's reasoning belongs next to the consumer that needs it.
---
